  "doc.title": "How Containers Isolate a Process · A Hands-on Essay",
  "doc.desc": "One docker run line spawns what looks like a fresh Linux box, yet there is no \"container\" struct anywhere in the Linux kernel. Following OCI Image 1.1 / Runtime 1.2 specs and Linux 6.x primitives, this essay takes that command apart: OCI layer SHA-256 ChainID deduplication, OverlayFS copy-up and .wh. whiteouts, eight Linux namespaces and Rootless UserNS UID mapping, veth bridges and NAT, cgroups v2 CPU throttling and unified memory OOM, seccomp-bpf and capabilities, PID 1 signals and zombie reaping, plus November 2026 frontiers in MicroVMs, EROFS, and WASI 0.3. Nine hands-on models cross-checked against Node crypto and exact spec arithmetic.",
